cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Semi-analytical methods for plates, shells and stiffened panels
type: software
abstract: >-
  The `panels` module provides semi-analytical (Ritz) models for plates,
  cylindrical shells and stiffened panels, single or multi-domain, using
  Bardell's hierarchical functions as approximation functions. Usually, this
  module is used for:

  * Linear static analyses

  * Linear buckling analyses

  * Frequency and panel flutter analyses

  * Geometrically non-linear static analyses, using the Newton-Raphson method
    or the arc-length methods of Riks and Crisfield

  * Multi-domain analyses of cylinders, stiffened panels and panels with
    debonding defects
